    "description": "Add shallow bundle support for large cases\n\n## What\n\n- `cloneCase` reads an optional `shallow` file in a case. When it is present, the eval fetches `repo.bundle` into an empty repo that holds the same shallow marks, because git refuses to clone a bundle made from a shallow repo.\n- `scripts/make-case.sh` writes `shallow` into the case when the source repo is shallow, and gives the bundle step the shallow marks so it does not stop at a missing object.\n- New `scripts/fetch-pr.sh <url> <merge-base> <head> <dir>`: a shallow repo that holds the merge base, the head and the commits between them, and nothing older.\n- README: the `shallow` file and the fetch script. Version 0.3.1.\n\n## Why\n\nD5 builds the first case set from Martian and ReviewBench. A full clone of sentry or cal.com makes a bundle of hundreds of megabytes. Two snapshots of the tree are 30 to 60 MB.\n\n## Tests\n\nTwo new tests in `test/eval-case.test.ts`: a shallow case checks out; the same bundle without the shallow file is rejected with the case name. Two in `test/eval-scripts.test.ts`: `fetch-pr.sh` then `make-case.sh` gives a case that `cloneCase` checks out with the three-dot diff available; `fetch-pr.sh` stops when the directory exists. `npm test` 1169 passed, lint, typecheck and build exit 0.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZgggAoxaZA98nRCMsW",
